  "body": "## What changed\n\n- On a machine of kind `Mill`, Detect holes does not store radial holes in the Drill op's `cross` list.\n- Each radial hole goes into `skipped`, with its size, origin and direction.\n- The Z holes stay in `holes`, and the op generates.\n- If no Z hole remains, Detect holes refuses. The refusal names each radial hole.\n- A lathe or a mill-turn keeps the old behaviour. The `cross` list is filled there.\n- The rule is in the new module `crates/app/src/operation/cross_reach.rs`. The test is the same `Kind::Mill` test that Generate uses for its \"no turret\" refusal.\n\n## Cause\n\n- #2601 made Detect holes store radial holes on every machine. Generate then refused them on a mill.\n- On a mill with Z holes and a radial hole, Generate refused with \"Z holes AND cross holes\".\n- `edit_operation` cannot clear `cross`, because the field is not in the params patch. The user could only delete the op.\n\n## Tests\n\n- New pin `drilling_detect_mill_radial::a_mill_skips_radial_holes_by_name_and_the_z_holes_generate`. The fixture is a plate with two D6 Z holes beside a bar with one blind D6 radial hole, on a mill, through MCP. The test expects `holes: 2`, `radial_holes: 0`, one `skipped` sentence, and a generate status of `ok`.\n- New pin `drilling_detect_mill_radial::a_mill_with_only_radial_holes_refuses_detection_by_name`.\n- Red before the fix: yes, both. Upstream answered `{\"holes\":2,\"radial_holes\":1,\"skipped\":[]}` (the issue's symptom).\n- Changed test `drilling_detect_opposite::mill_detection_names_opposite_blind_radial_holes_and_stores_none`. The #2601 test pinned the old behaviour. It now checks the two opposite blind holes through `cross_holes_of` (the #2601 recognizer coverage stays), and it checks the new mill refusal.\n- Mutation: with the old `material.rs` back, both new pins fail. With the fix restored, they pass.\n- Gate: the quick gate selects all 317 app suites for a lib change. That is far over the 5-minute budget. I ran the narrow ladder instead: the app lib tests and 30 suites that call `detect_holes` or do cross drilling (`mcp`, `drill_undersize`, `drilling_cross*`, `lathe_cross_drill`, `setup_align_*`, `bore_*`, `thread_*` and others). All are green. `camcraft-ui` lib `detect` tests: 7 green.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The issue's real STEP part on the Tormach 770MX + microARC 4 after `lay_part_on_face`. The pin uses a synthetic part on the default mill.\n- The full quick gate over all 317 app suites.\n- `cross` stays outside `edit_operation`. The issue accepts either fix. On a mill no `cross` list is filled now.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changes `material.rs` or the two test files. `material.rs` was 421 lines before this PR and is now 426. A split is a separate task.\n\nChangelog: Detect holes on a mill names each radial hole in `skipped` and keeps the Z holes, so the Drill op generates instead of refusing \"Z holes AND cross holes\".\n\nFixes #3448\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
